Toomey","displayName":"Travis Toomey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Shawn Oliver","displayName":"Shawn Oliver","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Ehlers’ power-play winner lifts Hurricanes past Jets 3-2 for 7th straight win","description":"— Nikolaj Ehlers scored a power-play goal 6:43 into the third period to lift the Carolina Hurricanes to their seventh straight victory, 3-2 over the Winnipeg Jets on Saturday.","story":"WINNIPEG, Manitoba -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114741/nikolaj-ehlers\">Nikolaj Ehlers</a> scored a power-play goal 6:43 into the third period to lift the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/car/carolina-hurricanes\">Carolina Hurricanes</a> to their seventh straight victory, 3-2 over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wpg/winnipeg-jets\">Winnipeg Jets</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              The former Jet fired a wrist shot past the glove of <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5104602/clay-stevenson\">Clay Stevenson</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976849/mark-jankowski\">Mark Jankowski</a> — also on the power play — and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4352692/jesperi-kotkaniemi\">Jesperi Kotkaniemi</a> scored for Carolina as well. Hurricanes defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3025662/shayne-gostisbehere\">Shayne Gostisbehere</a> had two assists.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565259/pyotr-kochetkov\">Pyotr Kochetkov</a> made 21 saves and has posted victories in all five starts this season. With fewer than 40 seconds remaining, Kochetkov made a pad save on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697392/cole-perfetti\">Cole Perfetti</a>, following that up with a save on 18-year-old <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5361711/viggo-bjorck\">Viggo Bjorck</a> off the helmet to preserve Carolina’s lead.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562632/mark-scheifele\">Mark Scheifele</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3652598/alex-iafallo\">Alex Iafallo</a> scored for Winnipeg, which lost its first game this season on home ice in regulation. Stevenson stopped 34 shots.\n\n\r\n              Winnipeg held 1-0 and 2-1 leads, before trailing in the third period. The Jets are 1-1 in matinee games this season, with nine more to play. After a three-game point drought to start the year, Scheifele is now riding a five-game point streak with two goals and six assists.\n\n\r\n              Carolina made the Jets pay on special-teams, scoring two goals while the power play and killing off Winnipeg’s lone opportunity with the man advantage. Jankowski’s second-period goal extended his NHL-leading active goal streak to seven consecutive games.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Jets: Visit the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/stl/st-louis-blues\">St. Louis Blues</a> on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Hurricanes: Visit the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cgy/calgary-flames\">Calgary Flames</a> on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-18T02:02:26Z"}}